    <bpmn:process id="W_W3796" name="W3796. Import Vendor Negotiation, FOB Pricing &amp; Cost-Reduction Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Sourcing cycle; cost-reduction target; contract renewal
Frequency: Annual + per negotiation
Volume: ~400 international vendors
Owner: Global Sourcing / Buyers
Participants: Global Sourcing, Buyers (links to VS-01/VS-19), Finance (links to VS-17.4/VS-106), Logistics Finance (links to W3788), Legal (links to VS-100.3), Merchandising (links to VS-01)
Source: workflow W3796 — Import Vendor Negotiation, FOB Pricing &amp; Cost-Reduction Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3796_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3796_Lane1" name="Global Sourcing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3796_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3796_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3796_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3796_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3796_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3796_Start3" name="Sourcing cycle; cost-reduction target; contract renewal">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3796_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3796_Task4" name="Global Sourcing/Buyers run import vendor negotiation: market price benchmarking…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Global Sourcing/Buyers run import vendor negotiation: market price benchmarking (FOB commodity indices links to VS-106), should-cost modeling, volume leverage and consolidated-buy negotiation across categories/entities, and Incoterms/payment-terms optimization (links to W3788)
Responsible (R): Global Sourcing / Buyers / Finance
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Annual + per deal</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3796_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3796_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3796_Task5" name="Global Sourcing/Legal document pricing in contracts/schedules (links to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Global Sourcing/Legal document pricing in contracts/schedules (links to W688/VS-100.3): price-adjustment mechanism (raw-material index, FX clause), volume tiers, and rebate/incentive (links to VS-39)
